In simple words, the demon slayer folder is a playable 3D boss-fight mini-game prototype called Kaalyuga: The Bleeding Crown.
Here is what it is and how it works:
1. What the Game Is
The Fight: You play as Rudra, a warrior armed with a glowing battle-axe (Parashu), fighting a giant horned bull-demon boss named Dundubhi inside a burning stone temple courtyard.
The Art Style: It is styled like the anime Demon Slayer — 3D characters have bold black ink outlines, bright comic/anime shading, and dramatic elemental trails (fire, lightning, and wind) flying off your axe when you swing.
2. How You Play
Move & Dodge: Use WASD (or Arrow keys) to run around the isometric arena and Space to dash with afterimages.
Attack Combos:
Left Click / J: 3-hit light axe combo.
Right Click / K: Slow heavy slam that shoots out 3 crescent energy waves.
Q or E: Special 360° Astra Cyclone spin attack (has a 4.5-second cooldown).
3 Elemental Styles (Keys 1, 2, 3):
1 — Agni (Fire): Hits hardest.
2 — Vajra (Lightning): Fastest swings & breaks the boss's balance faster.
3 — Vayu (Wind): Longest attack reach.
Block & Perfect Parry (Shift or L): Holding block reduces damage, but tapping block right before Dundubhi hits you triggers a Deflect (sparks, metallic clash sound, zero damage, and builds up stun on the boss).
Use the Pillars: There are stone pillars in the arena. If you bait Dundubhi into bull-charging into a pillar, the pillar shatters, deals huge damage to him, and stuns him so you can land bonus hits.
Phase 2: When Dundubhi drops below 55% health, he roars, enters Phase 2, glows brighter red, and attacks faster.
3. Clever Tricks Used Under the Hood
Video + 3D Hybrid Stage: Instead of building a heavy 3D temple from scratch, the game plays a looping video (dundubhi_chamber.mp4) as the floor/background and lines up a transparent 3D Three.js camera on top of it so the 3D characters, shadows, and pillars sit naturally in the room.
Smart 3D Model Cleanup (assetLoader.ts): The raw 3D character models (.fbx) are super heavy (hundreds of thousands of triangles), so the code automatically simplifies them when loading, fixes their textures, keeps their feet planted on the ground (Y = 0), and trims the animations so attacks feel snappy.
Anime VFX (slashRibbonVfx.ts & vfxFlipbook.ts):
Sword Trails: Tracks the base and tip of Rudra's axe every frame to draw smooth glowing ink-and-element ribbons in the air.
2D Sprite Effects: Explosions, blood crescents, dust clouds, shockwaves, and ground cracks are drawn using pre-made anime sprite-sheet PNGs placed in 3D space.
Juice & Sound (soundEngine.ts, GameHud.tsx): Screen shake, brief freeze-frames on big hits ("hitstop"), floating damage numbers, background music, drum hits, and synthesized sword/parry sound effects.
Tests: Two test files (rules.test.ts and slashRibbonVfx.test.ts) check that movement, combos, parries, pillar collisions, and visual trails work properly.
4. Folder Layout at a Glance
app/ — Entry page and fonts/styles.
components/game/ — The title screen (TitleOverlay.tsx), health bars/UI (GameHud.tsx), and the main 3D game screen (KaalyugaStage.tsx).
lib/game/ — All game rules, boss AI, shaders, 3D model loader, arena props, slash effects, and sound engine.
public/kaalyuga/ — All 3D models, animations, background video, music/SFX, and anime VFX sprite sheets.
